t (b\\times c) & =⟨3,5,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6+5\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =18-5-12 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106135 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e0b4d33-7699-5068-90f1-663534cd662d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Scalar Triple Products Using Its Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e8bb8d9-a3bb-5f41-8ede-1ac64d1b2be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285210} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6f5fc5-825c-54cb-8f8c-ee058c85459b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286501} {:answer/id #uuid "eef31947-0a99-57ff-8618-686a5c2e30a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286986} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a78fa7-b3e6-5170-9dc3-909924cfd396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,0,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287024} {:answer/id #uuid "f992ea26-69d2-5514-84ea-1987e40856cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb6f5fc5-825c-54cb-8f8c-ee058c85459b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286501} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffd48eaf-9d9e-5aaf-ad75-c7d452ae0613" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0db80f94-e2a5-583e-875d-ce7dd7157cf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-20062" :question/problem "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a)$, if $b\\times c=⟨2,3,0⟩$ and $a=⟨1,-2,2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨1,-2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2-6+0 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff317cd2-0896-5134-b3a3-4e9f84e22b68" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Scalar Triple Product Using a Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05a8d4cf-2a52-5eb3-932c-de54f969d498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339182} {:answer/id #uuid "3c2029a1-5daa-5d17-915b-5cb3db9d0a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339671} {:answer/id #uuid "7364ef2c-a924-50d5-ae40-c9a6106f8bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340158} {:answer/id #uuid "84d38775-5cfe-5497-a2ea-945dc01057b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340327} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f005ac-dfb9-5a8e-9f29-140e8e17a482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84d38775-5cfe-5497-a2ea-945dc01057b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340327} :answer-field/id #uuid "50438105-46e0-54c5-8329-966f684eb5e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc420fe9-802f-5344-9de7-9b53d8435b37" :question/math-academy-id "q-73462" :question/problem "Let $p=⟨3,1,2⟩$, $q=⟨1,-2,1⟩$ and $r=⟨4,1,-2⟩.$ Find $r\\cdot (q\\times p).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $r\\cdot (q\\times p)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $r,$ $q,$ and $p.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot (q\\times p) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4((-2)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-(1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3)-2(1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-20+1-14 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
